Real world application 2: 🖥️ Server Log Analyzer

📌 Brief Description

The Server Log Analyzer is a C++ program that reads a server log file and identifies important ERROR and CRITICAL messages.

The program processes the log line by line, searches for error-related keywords, stores matching entries, and displays a report of critical events.

🔑 Key Concepts

- 📂 File reading
- 📝 Line-by-line processing
- 🔎 String searching using "find()"
- 📦 "vector" for storing log entries
- 🛡️ Defensive error handling
- 📊 Critical-event reporting

🌍 Real-World Application

This concept is useful in DevOps monitoring, server administration, application debugging, system monitoring, and failure analysis.

🎯 Main Purpose

To demonstrate how log files can be automatically analyzed to identify errors and critical system events quickly.
